window.EN={"1":"Taking Dorias's counsel, Leif and his army make for Leonster along the coast.","2":"But to reach Leonster by this highway,","3":"they must break through an imperial fort called \"Fort Norden.\"","4":"There, an elite Friege corps had been deployed, seeking to block the \"Liberation Army's\" advance.","5":"Kempf, your preparations are complete, I trust.","6":"Leave it to me, General Nikalaf. They style themselves a liberation army, but their fighting strength is beneath that of bandits.","7":"With my army alone I shall crush them with ease.","8":"\"With ease,\" you say? Hold your tongue, boy!!","9":"Who was it who, though in charge of Fort Dandrum, abandoned his men and came shamelessly running back alone!","10":"They are the Lanzenritter of Leonster.","11":"With Prince Leif as their leader, and with their homeland before their eyes, their morale all but reaches the heavens.","12":"Take them lightly and you will be inviting death!","13":"Sir... My apologies...","14":"Your unit is to defend the bridge here to the death. The ballista units will support you from the rear.","15":"I will not permit you to fight outside their range! Understand, this is an order!!","16":"Sir...","17":"The all-out attack comes after the reinforcements from Ulster arrive. We pincer them front and rear and smash the enemy in one stroke.","18":"Reinforcements from Ulster?","19":"Yes. Count Conomor is coming with about a hundred riders.","20":"The enemy will be attacked from behind by the strongest corps in northern Thracia.","21":"I see... But then it won't be my achievement...","22":"I'd like somehow to take them down with my own hands...","23":"Prince, word from the soldiers sent ahead. The enemy's formation is like this.","24":"A large ballista force around Fort Norden... Unless we do something about that, we can't take the fort.","25":"To cross to the far side of the river, we have no choice but to seize this bridge.","26":"However, an armored corps is holding it firmly, and fighting within the shooters' range puts us at a disadvantage.","27":"Which means we just have to lure this armored corps out of range.","28":"However, I do not think the enemy will move so easily.","29":"But I think it's worth considering. There must be some way...","30":"Lord Leif, please give that task to me. I know that commander. I can lure him off the bridge.","31":"You, Olwen!? No. I can't let you do something so dangerous.","32":"Please. I want to be of use to you, Prince!!","33":"Father, it seems a battle is about to begin outside. It's dangerous to go out now. Please rest in this house a while longer.","34":"Yes. Then I shall accept your kindness...","35":"Tch... Why do I have to be the vanguard for an idiot like that?","36":"So a commoner like me is, in the end, nothing more than a shield for the nobles...","37":"Good, all troops charge as one. Fight in a way that does honor to the name of Ulster!!","38":"Lord Conomor, is this truly all right? Win or lose, we will lose our homeland.","39":"If we lose this opportunity, there will never again be a chance to retake our homeland...","40":"I know.","41":"But if we turn traitor, Princess Miranda, who is being held hostage, will lose her life.","42":"The princess is still fifteen... Do you not think she is far too young to end her life in that dark monastery...","43":"Hey, hey, mister...","44":"What? Who are you? Stop scurrying around in front of me!","45":"Hey, please, won't you take our side?","46":"Hey, hey, what are you coming out with so abruptly?","47":"You're a weird one, honestly...","48":"No good after all? ...Well, I figured it'd be a no.","49":"Okay then. Goodbye...","50":"Hey! Wait a second!","51":"What?","52":"Fine. Depending on the terms, I might switch sides.","53":"Really! So, what are the terms?","54":"Let's see. If Leonster is restored, how about making me a noble?","55":"I think that'd be easy, but do you want to be a noble?","56":"Are you a commoner, by any chance? Then you're a real hard worker.","57":"A commoner who's a senior knight is rare in the Friege army.","58":"Stop saying commoner, commoner!","59":"Yes! I'm commoner-born all right, but it's not as if I'm ashamed of it.","60":"I take pride in being a commoner!","61":"Then there's no need to become a noble.","62":"Well... that's true, but... never mind about that!","63":"My name's Karin. What's your name?","64":"I-I'm Ilios...","65":"The name alone sounds really noble. Is it a fake name, by any chance?","66":"Don't be stupid! It's not a fake name!","67":"It's the name my old man gave me because he looked up to nobles. It's my real name!!","68":"Then your noble complex is because of that name.","69":"I think you should change it. Not Ilios; make it Olson.","70":"That definitely suits you better.","71":"O-Olson...!? Hey, don't go changing a person's name on your own...","72":"Okay then, Mr. Olson, we're comrades from now on. Nice to meet you!","73":"H-hey...","74":"General Kempf. It has been a while.","75":"You're Olwen!? You traitor!!","76":"If I am a traitor, then you are a beaten dog. No, a coward.","77":"Wh-what!! How am I a coward!","78":"You don't have the courage to fight, do you? I hear you ran about at Dandrum, too.","79":"Even now you're only hiding in your soldiers' shadow and trembling.","80":"Like that, you'll never beat my brother Reinhardt, not ever!","81":"Grrr... If I let you go on!!","82":"Someone! Seize this woman!! I'll kill you all, every last one... I'll kill you!!!","83":"Lord Leif, my task is done... I wish you fortune in battle...","84":"Hey, order all troops to charge! Tell them whoever takes an enemy head gets a bounty!","85":"Cut them down to the last one!","86":"P-please wait, General! That goes against General Nikalaf's order!","87":"As long as we win, anything can be smoothed over. Have you forgotten that my house belongs to the royal family!","88":"All troops! Charge!! Cut down the enemy, don't let a single one escape!!!","89":"...As expected of the Lanzenritter of Leonster. It would be wiser to pull back for now...","90":"All troops, we now move to withdraw!","91":"Ah, you are Lord Leif!","92":"Yes. The priest of Solwood told me to meet you.","93":"But how did you know?","94":"It is as I saw at the Tower of Bragi... The boy who bears the light of Zwei... a great power...","95":"Lord Claud... It is just as you said...","96":"The Tower of Bragi? The light of Zwei? What on earth do you mean?","97":"When the time comes, you will understand.","98":"Prince Leif, I shall accompany you for a while. That is acceptable, yes?","99":"The Father is resting. He says he doesn't wish to see anyone.","100":"Honestly, ever since this area was incorporated into the Kingdom of North Thracia, nothing good has come of it.","101":"I miss the days of Leonster...","102":"Back then I'd go far off to find work, but now you can't even travel in peace.","103":"I don't need it anymore, so I'll give you this key.","104":"What, you people are connected to Leonster?","105":"Then it'll be the age of the Kingdom of Leonster again.","106":"This is holy water. Please use it. I don't need any thanks. We want to be of use too!","107":"I hear you folks are fighting to liberate this Thracia.","108":"I'll give you this \"Knight's Crest,\" so keep at it until the day Thracia is liberated.","109":"Prince, splendidly done. You have triumphed well over this difficult situation.","110":"Your homeland Leonster is before your eyes. The people have long awaited your return.","111":"Leonster... my homeland...","112":"Indeed. You were still small, Prince, so you may not remember it, but...","113":"I remember. That night especially, I'll never forget as long as I live.","114":"That night?","115":"The night Leonster fell... The sky was bright red with soaring flames.","116":"In Finn's arms, I just stared blankly up at the sky.","117":"At first I didn't really understand.","118":"But when I saw Finn's face, a deep sorrow suddenly welled up in me.","119":"It was the first time in my life I had ever felt so sad...","120":"I pushed a painful duty onto Finn. But there was no one but him to whom I could entrust you.","121":"As long as the prince is safe, Leonster will rise again someday without fail.","122":"Telling him that, I had him escape from the burning castle.","123":"That day was the last time I saw Finn's tears.","124":"Since then, he seems to have forgotten how to cry... no, even how to smile...","125":"His heart is surely still in Leonster.","126":"No, not only his. We all left our hearts behind in Leonster...","127":"But when Ulster's army appeared from behind, honestly, I wondered what would become of us.","128":"The enemy's lack of coordination saved us.","129":"But that is Count Conomor for you.","130":"The swiftness with which he gathered his soldiers the moment he saw the odds were against him was admirable, enemy though he is.","131":"Count Conomor?","132":"Ulster's finest brave general, an excellent knight with more than his share of devotion to righteousness and of patriotism for his homeland.","133":"Why would such a man side with the Empire?","134":"Doesn't he want to do something about this imperial tyranny?","135":"He must have circumstances that leave him no choice...","136":"In any case, there is no doubt he is an opponent I would not wish to fight a second time.","137":"Damn it, if only you weren't here... if only you weren't heeere!","138":"Absurd... M-me... to the likes of them...","139":"Curse you... I won't forget this! Remember that!","140":"You rebels! Take my blade, if you can!","141":"Guh... This is... not the end...","142":"So even I am made light of...","143":"You mean to fight me?","144":"Hmph, interesting. Can you defeat the great Ilios!","145":"So I end up finishing as a commoner after all...","146":"Tch... Working me to the bone because they think I'm just a commoner...","147":"I can't take this anymore.","148":"I bear you no grudge, but this too is fate. Forgive me!","149":"May Ulster... rise... once again...","150":"Mmh... Must I live on in shame..."};
